        <mxCell id="ac_note_parallel" parent="1" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;align=left;spacingLeft=6;fontSize=11;" value="tuner1_parallel.py runs the same flow with tune_ticker() fanned across a ProcessPoolExecutor (one worker/core); writes tuning_…_parallel.csv. tuner_analysis.py is the offline step: reloads a tuning CSV and draws plot_2d / plot_3d — no backtests, no Alpaca. TUNE_DIRECTIONAL=True (both tuners): tune_ticker() instead runs 2 independent sweeps per vol_len — long entries (short disabled) and short entries (long disabled) via check_vol_price_body_dir(), tagging every result 'direction': 'long'/'short' — 32,400 combos/ticker vs. 16,200 for the shared-params grid above." vertex="1">
